00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:52,340
That's Atsumumiya's serve

280
00:13:52,340 --> 00:13:53,820
It's awesome

281
00:13:53,820 --> 00:13:55,640
Yeah I'm sorry

282
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:57,560
I completely suck at encouraging other people

283
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:59,900
I'm too busy dealing with my own stuff

284
00:13:59,900 --> 00:14:04,140
I'll just deal with me

285
00:14:04,140 --> 00:14:06,980
No matter what the pass

286
00:14:06,980 --> 00:14:09,220
I'll get points

287
00:14:09,220 --> 00:14:20,640
I don't need A-passes either

288
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:21,920
Just get them to me high

289
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:23,600
Wow

290
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:26,980
Listen Kageyama

291
00:14:26,980 --> 00:14:28,840
We need to talk about your timing

292
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:29,720
Huh?

293
00:14:29,900 --> 00:14:30,980
What's your problem?

294
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:32,400
Great speech Asahi

295
00:14:32,400 --> 00:14:33,100
Yeah?

296
00:14:33,340 --> 00:14:34,660
I think it kind of fell apart

297
00:14:34,660 --> 00:14:36,780
Atsumu

298
00:14:36,780 --> 00:14:40,360
You saw Karasuno's setter serve earlier

299
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:42,740
And now you want to do a spike serve right?

300
00:14:43,860 --> 00:14:47,320
You think it'd be so much cooler to just blast a spike serve past him

301
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:49,400
And you're tired of jump floaters

302
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:51,720
How does he know?

303
00:14:52,380 --> 00:14:54,400
Your jump floaters are scoring well right now

304
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:57,040
If you're gonna crush their libero

305
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:58,280
Then go crush him

306
00:14:58,280 --> 00:14:59,660
Yes sir

307
00:14:59,660 --> 00:15:04,580
The ultimate challenger in Nadazaki

308
00:15:04,580 --> 00:15:06,360
Alright let's go

309
00:15:06,360 --> 00:15:07,160
Yeah

310
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:11,200
Or the unknown old contender Karasuno

311
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:13,940
Which team will reach the top first?

312
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:18,240
This fateful third set starts off with a serve from Atsumumiya

313
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:43,880
How many is that now?

314
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:46,500
That's big time server Atsumumiya

315
00:15:46,500 --> 00:15:50,260
Starting off the third set with a service ace right from the get-go

316
00:15:50,260 --> 00:15:53,500
I was sure it was going out myself

317
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:55,460
Atsumu is really on his game today

318
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:57,960
I bet he could score with a spike serve if he tried

319
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:58,980
Sure

320
00:15:58,980 --> 00:16:02,600
The chances of him getting it over are basically equal either way

321
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:03,240
Hmm?

322
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:05,920
Didn't you just tell him to stick with jump floaters?

323
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:09,020
Both of Atsumu's serves are extremely powerful

324
00:16:09,020 --> 00:16:10,120
But

325
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:13,620
If he switches to a spike serve and the other team manages to get it

326
00:16:13,620 --> 00:16:16,320
He'll end up thinking that he should have gone with the jump float serve

327
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:18,060
And that will stick with him the rest of the game

328
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:19,920
Whereas

329
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:22,680
If he hits a really good jump floater and they get it

330
00:16:22,680 --> 00:16:24,500
Knowing Atsumu's personality

331
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:26,460
It would rev up his competitive side

332
00:16:26,460 --> 00:16:27,760
And get him to play even harder

333
00:16:27,760 --> 00:16:29,680
So as far as this match goes

334
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:32,540
I think sticking to jump floaters is a better choice

335
00:16:32,540 --> 00:16:33,820
To keep him engaged

336
00:16:33,820 --> 00:16:37,380
The weird part is he's always right about this stuff

337
00:16:37,380 --> 00:16:53,240
I feel like my feet are nailed to the floor

338
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:56,200
I can tell I'm responding slower than usual

339
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:58,000
Oh yeah

340
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:59,440
This is it

341
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:01,580
This is what fear feels like

342
00:17:01,580 --> 00:17:03,240
I'm on the left side

343
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:04,240
Asahi!

344
00:17:04,240 --> 00:17:05,240
Yes!

345
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:06,240
Nice kill, man!

346
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:10,240
Wow, look at that Asahi's being all dependable

347
00:17:10,240 --> 00:17:11,240
Nishinoi is human

348
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:14,240
He has the right to get overwhelmed every once in a while too

349
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:18,240
It looks to me like Karasuno switched their rotation up

350
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:21,160
It looks to me like Karasuno switched their rotation up

351
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:25,960
Subaru, feel free to share your expert commentary

352
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:26,860
Huh?

353
00:17:27,300 --> 00:17:28,560
Oh, I, uh

354
00:17:28,560 --> 00:17:31,900
If there's one thing that makes volleyball's rules unique

355
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:34,060
I'd say it's the player rotation system

356
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:37,560
That's where, whenever the team gets a new turn at serving

357
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:40,240
All the players have to rotate positions clockwise

358
00:17:40,240 --> 00:17:43,700
Each team decides their starting order before a set

359
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:45,120
And submits it to the organizers

360
00:17:45,120 --> 00:17:49,620
For example, one common rotation is for the setter to start off in the back row

361
00:17:49,620 --> 00:17:54,320
Using that combination means there will be three solid attackers up front right off the bat

362
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:57,380
It's also pretty common to start off with the strongest server

363
00:17:57,380 --> 00:18:00,820
For Narazaki, their setter is also their best server

364
00:18:00,820 --> 00:18:02,700
So they get both strategies at once

365
00:18:02,700 --> 00:18:07,580
Which means this is probably a permanent starting rotation for them

366
00:18:07,580 --> 00:18:10,000
They're telling opponents to try whatever they want

367
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,220
We have a rotation that works no matter what

368
00:18:12,220 --> 00:18:13,160
And here it is

369
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:17,600
On the other hand, Karasuno feels like a team that just dives in head first

370
00:18:17,600 --> 00:18:21,220
But they also seem like the type to actually use a lot of trial and error

371
00:18:21,220 --> 00:18:24,720
Narazaki seems pretty evenly strong in any rotation

372
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:29,880
But I'm guessing their attack stat is highest when number 4, number 10, and number 11 are up front

373
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:32,100
Karasuno's strengths are more polarized

374
00:18:32,100 --> 00:18:34,700
Especially their middle blocker spot

375
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:37,380
Their mini number 10 is so specialized in attack

376
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:38,500
They can put him anywhere

377
00:18:38,500 --> 00:18:39,540
And he doesn't care

378
00:18:39,540 --> 00:18:41,120
He'll be a point-scoring machine

379
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:43,460
He's also a very effective decoy

380
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:46,920
Their four-eyed number 11 seems to be the keystone of their defense

381
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:50,040
So you'd want to put him wherever the other team's attackers are strongest

382
00:18:50,040 --> 00:18:55,580
No, maybe they should be putting everything they have into shutting down the serve for Matsumumiya

383
00:18:55,580 --> 00:18:58,760
But doing that, they couldn't start with a power server

384
00:18:58,760 --> 00:19:01,640
The setter or the samurai

385
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:06,880
Nobody likes a blabbermouth know-it-all

386
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:09,580
Sorry, I've been talking way too much

387
00:19:09,580 --> 00:19:11,340
I think I've got this part

388
00:19:11,340 --> 00:19:15,180
If Inarizaki is in the same rotation but Karasuno changed theirs

389
00:19:15,180 --> 00:19:18,800
That means when players from Inarizaki attack

390
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:22,220
They'll be in the same position but up against new Karasuno blockers

391
00:19:22,220 --> 00:19:24,140
That's it! Exactly right!

392
00:19:24,140 --> 00:19:25,900
All the matchups are going to be different

393
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:27,820
Every time the rotations change

394
00:19:27,820 --> 00:19:30,340
We'll get to see a different little battle play out

395
00:19:30,340 --> 00:19:31,340
Alan!

396
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:31,980
Got it!

397
00:19:33,320 --> 00:19:36,100
Karasuno has already picked off Ojiro with their serve

398
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:39,120
A super-fast quick attack!

399
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:41,240
One touch!

400
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:42,920
Yes!

401
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:45,880
How does it help for you to freak out?

402
00:19:46,300 --> 00:19:48,800
I'm betting this is why Karasuno chose this rotation

403
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:50,800
The way things are now

404
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:53,940
The twins' quick attack will keep matching up with old four-eyes

405
00:19:53,940 --> 00:19:56,880
Alright, let's switch up our rotation

406
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:58,900
When Matsumumiya is serving

407
00:19:58,900 --> 00:20:01,340
He's gonna aim at Nishinoya every single time

408
00:20:01,340 --> 00:20:03,400
Whether he's positioned in the middle or not

409
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:05,520
Ha! Obsessed much?

410
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:10,100
Tsukishima, I'm gonna have you match up with Osamumiya and Rintaro Tsuna more often

411
00:20:10,100 --> 00:20:13,020
Countering the twins quick

412
00:20:13,020 --> 00:20:16,580
Yeah, because that was the biggest surprise we've had to deal with from them

413
00:20:16,580 --> 00:20:19,260
We're counting on you, you weirdo quick killer

414
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:21,580
Uh, okay

415
00:20:21,580 --> 00:20:25,200
The Hinata Inuoka strategy was actually working pretty good

416
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:30,660
But unfortunately, I think Tanaka's getting tired of always having to jump up to block in Hinata's place

417
00:20:30,660 --> 00:20:33,780
I'd honestly like to tell you it's all good

418
00:20:33,780 --> 00:20:35,280
But being in the middle sucks

419
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:40,860
So Tsukishima, jealous I got put in charge of something important?

420
00:20:41,700 --> 00:20:45,020
Uh-oh, looks like I just stole your big important job

421
00:20:45,020 --> 00:20:50,300
Tsukishima never neglects his trash talk

422
00:20:50,300 --> 00:20:51,400
The guy's a pro

423
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:53,100
It's an art form, really

424
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:59,140
Samu, look!

425
00:21:06,020 --> 00:21:06,580
Alex!

426
00:21:08,580 --> 00:21:11,720
Ojiro is definitely the guy we need to keep from getting hot

427
00:21:11,720 --> 00:21:14,200
So for this third set

428
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:17,300
I want to put one more blocker in his way

429
00:21:17,300 --> 00:21:30,820
And he is shut down

430
00:21:30,820 --> 00:21:36,600
First-year Tobio Kageyama blocked Inanazaki's ace, Alen Ojiro, all on his own

431
00:21:36,600 --> 00:21:39,840
Karasuno takes the lead with a brilliant play

432
00:21:39,840 --> 00:21:43,860
That announces to the world that this will not be a repeat of the second set

433
00:21:43,860 --> 00:21:50,100
Nationals has always had some amazing blockers

434
00:21:50,100 --> 00:21:54,520
I couldn't even tell you how many times I've been shut down

435
00:21:54,520 --> 00:21:58,160
They come at me so fast, it's like I'm frozen in time

436
00:21:58,160 --> 00:22:01,940
Sometimes they're in front of me before I can even try to attack

437
00:22:01,940 --> 00:22:06,380
Those hands stretching out over me are sheer terror incarnate

438
00:22:06,380 --> 00:22:12,440
In fact, a block that doesn't scare the crap out of you isn't a real block at all

439
00:22:12,440 --> 00:22:14,980
Who knew a setter

440
00:22:14,980 --> 00:22:19,200
Would be an even more terrifying blocker than Four Eyes over there

441
00:22:19,200 --> 00:22:25,680
確かなことはいつか

442
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:28,500
分かる時が来るから

443
00:22:28,500 --> 00:22:31,060
間違ったっていいさ

444
00:22:31,060 --> 00:22:35,080
今思いを止めないで

445
00:22:35,080 --> 00:22:49,540
現実が飛んじゃうような

446
00:22:49,540 --> 00:22:52,460
夢が欲しかったのに

447
00:22:52,460 --> 00:22:57,040
辻褄を合わすだけの日々は

448
00:22:57,040 --> 00:22:58,700
味気ない

449
00:22:58,700 --> 00:23:01,780
何にも怖くなんて泣いて

450
00:23:01,780 --> 00:23:04,940
強がって馬鹿の少年が

451
00:23:04,940 --> 00:23:10,780
今もまだ汗ばむ背中を見つめてるから

452
00:23:10,780 --> 00:23:14,040
奇跡はもういらない

453
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:17,520
どこまでだって

454
00:23:17,520 --> 00:23:20,460
いける僕らはファンで

455
00:23:20,460 --> 00:23:22,380
夢も叶うさ

456
00:23:22,380 --> 00:23:25,280
ここまでやってきたのは

457
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:28,280
偶然なんかじゃなくて

458
00:23:28,280 --> 00:23:31,440
さてしまう舞台に

459
00:23:31,440 --> 00:23:32,320
だって

460
00:23:32,320 --> 00:23:34,140
痛いといつでも

461
00:23:34,140 --> 00:23:37,200
強く願い続けた

462
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:40,280
君がそこにいたから

463
00:23:40,280 --> 00:23:54,280
次回は

464
00:23:54,280 --> 00:23:55,040
HERO

465
00:23:55,040 --> 00:23:58,720
スピード

466
00:23:58,860 --> 00:24:00,200
アーレーン

